# PROJECT_NAME — agent context

> Generated by `orch init --template chatbot-whatsapp` (GENERATED_AT).

## About orch (this project is orch-managed)

- `orch` walks `tasks.json` as a DAG and dispatches each task to
  Claude / Codex / OpenCode / Gemini in parallel.
- **CLI missing?** `pipx install orch`
  (repo: <https://github.com/hectorcanaimero/orch>).
- **Never edit `tasks.json` status directly** — runtime state lives in
  SQLite. Use `orch task set --id ID --status STATUS` or one of the
  `scripts/task-*.sh` helpers.
- **Full agent context on demand**: if you use Claude Code, run
  `orch install-skills` once — the `/orch` skill loads only when the
  agent needs it (token-cheap). Otherwise `orch --help` is the source
  of truth.

## Stack

- Python `>=3.11`
- FastAPI `>=0.115,<0.116` (pin the ceiling — Starlette 1.0 breaks the legacy `TemplateResponse`)
- `uvicorn[standard]` for the dev server
- **Waha** (`devlikeapro/waha`) as the self-hosted WhatsApp HTTP API — runs via docker-compose
- `anthropic>=0.40` — Claude SDK for the agent loop
- Dev: `pytest`, `ruff`, `httpx`

## Layout

- `app/main.py` — FastAPI app; exposes `POST /webhook` and boots the agent.
- `app/agent.py` — Claude client wrapper; owns per-chat context.
- `app/store/` — event log + per-chat conversation state (JSONL for now).
- `app/prompts/system.md` — the system prompt Claude gets on every reply.
- `docker-compose.yml` — Waha service. Bring it up with `make waha-up`.
- `.orchestrator/` — orch state (config, model router, SQLite).

## Conventions

- **Never log message bodies at INFO level.** WhatsApp conversations are private. Use DEBUG or redact `payload.body` before logging.
- **Always validate the `X-Api-Key` header** on `/webhook` — Waha proxies unauthenticated traffic if you don't.
- **Reply-back errors are silent-fail** — a broken Claude call must NOT leave the webhook hanging. Return 200 to Waha and log the failure.
- **Every new route ships with a test in the same PR.** No exceptions.
- Run `pytest -q` before pushing; the shipped CI workflow runs the same command.

## Orch state

- SQLite at `.orchestrator/state/PROJECT_NAME/orch.db`.
- `tasks_definition` (static): id, model, backend, deps, phase, estimate.
- `tasks_runtime` (dynamic): status, attempts, last_model, last_backend.
- **Never edit runtime status in `tasks.json`** — use `orch task set --id ID --status STATUS` instead.

## Useful commands

```bash
make waha-up                              # start the Waha container
uvicorn app.main:app --reload             # dev server
orch status                               # human table of tasks
orch tasks --status todo,in-progress      # narrower view
orch run --dry-run                        # preview the plan
orch dashboard --profile stakeholder      # share the URL with your client
```

## Sending to Waha

Reply back to a chat with:

```python
import httpx, os
httpx.post(
    f"{os.environ['WAHA_URL']}/api/sendText",
    headers={"X-Api-Key": os.environ["WAHA_API_KEY"]},
    json={"session": "default", "chatId": chat_id, "text": text},
    timeout=10,
)
```

WhatsApp rate-limits at ~1 msg/sec per chat — the SDK doesn't debounce for you.
